| Intentional element identified (literal excerpt)                                                                  | Class    | Justification                                                                                                                                                                |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| “deliver food from the kitchen to an inpatient room”                                                              | Goal     | This describes the desired state the system should achieve: food reaches the inpatient room. It does not by itself prescribe exactly how the delivery must be performed.     |
| “delivery is made on an order-by-order basis in response to kitchen delivery requests”                            | Task     | This specifies a particular operational way of performing food delivery: deliveries are triggered by kitchen requests and handled per order.                                 |
| “delivered into a room table by the robot”                                                                        | Task     | This is a specific way of achieving food delivery: the robot places the food on the room table.                                                                              |
| “requires a special manipulation robot skill”                                                                     | Resource | The manipulation skill is an available capability required for the robot to perform table delivery. The concern is whether that capability is available.                     |
| “food can be fetched from the robot's tray”                                                                       | Task     | This is an alternative concrete way of completing delivery: the food is retrieved from the robot’s tray rather than placed by the robot.                                     |
| “requires cooperation with the inpatient, a companion, a nurse, or another robot”                                 | Resource | The cooperation of another party is a required availability condition for this delivery alternative. The concern is whether a suitable cooperating participant is available. |
| “Some inpatients could be unable to fetch the food from the tray”                                                 | Belief   | This captures a domain assumption/rationale that affects design decisions about whether tray fetching is feasible.                                                           |
| “a companion visitor or nurse could not be available at the moment of the delivery”                               | Belief   | This is a domain characteristic explaining why the system cannot always rely on human assistance during delivery.                                                            |
| “information about if the inpatient, a companion visitor or nurse can be able to retrieve the food from the tray” | Resource | This is an informational entity needed by the system to decide whether tray retrieval is possible.                                                                           |
| “inpatient record”                                                                                                | Resource | The inpatient record is an informational resource used to obtain patient-related delivery feasibility information.                                                           |
| “information about the patient”                                                                                   | Resource | This is informational input used to determine whether the patient can retrieve food from the tray.                                                                           |
| “presence of a companion into the room”                                                                           | Resource | This is information about the availability of a potential helper, which is needed to decide whether cooperative retrieval is possible.                                       |
| “This information is subject to uncertainty”                                                                      | Belief   | This represents design rationale about the reliability of the available information and affects decision-making under uncertainty.                                           |
| “carry multiple meals”                                                                                            | Task     | This specifies a particular operational capability or process the robot performs during delivery.                                                                            |
| “indicate which meal should be retrieved by a given inpatient”                                                    | Goal     | This describes a required system outcome: the correct meal is identified for the correct inpatient during retrieval.                                                         |
| “track when and where each meal was retrieved”                                                                    | Goal     | This states a functional requirement the system should achieve: maintaining retrieval time and location traceability.                                                        |
| “alert if a wrong meal is retrieved”                                                                              | Goal     | This describes a desired system condition or behavior: detecting and notifying about incorrect meal retrieval.                                                               |
| “Dirty dishes should be retrieved from the room”                                                                  | Goal     | This expresses a desired state of affairs: dirty dishes are removed from the inpatient room.                                                                                 |
| “the dish retrieve can occur unassisted”                                                                          | Task     | This is one specific way of performing dish retrieval, without cooperation from other actors.                                                                                |
| “with the cooperation of two robots”                                                                              | Task     | This is a specific operational alternative for retrieving dishes using two cooperating robots.                                                                               |
| “with the cooperation of robots and a human”                                                                      | Task     | This is another concrete way of performing dish retrieval, involving both robots and a human.                                                                                |
| “Opening the room door”                                                                                           | Task     | This is a concrete action needed to support delivery or dish retrieval.                                                                                                      |
| “cooperation with another robot or a human”                                                                       | Resource | The availability of another robot or human is required for opening the room door in some cases.                                                                              |
| “Someone in the room can call a robot to pick up the dishes”                                                      | Task     | This specifies a particular interaction process for initiating dish pickup: a person calls the robot.                                                                        |
| “that person can signal if they can open the door when the robot comes to it”                                     | Task     | This specifies a concrete communication action that supports the robot’s door-opening coordination.                                                                          |

